WEBVTT

00:37.954 --> 00:43.250
In the 19th century, as America expanded
across the vast continent,

00:43.251 --> 00:46.963
the frontier was, without a doubt,
the conquest of the West.

00:52.010 --> 00:53.219
To the West…

00:57.098 --> 00:59.893
a desire called America
crossed the continent…

01:02.937 --> 01:05.315
consuming the lands of the native people

01:06.232 --> 01:08.318
and reaching the Pacific Ocean.

01:18.203 --> 01:20.245
Punish him! We must punish him!

01:20.246 --> 01:23.416
He had the white man's books
hidden in his tent!

01:32.467 --> 01:34.344
What's with that way of running?

01:35.011 --> 01:37.097
That's how white men run!

01:39.432 --> 01:41.226
He disappeared?!

01:45.105 --> 01:50.860
And in the summer of 1890,
people began to gather in the wilderness,

01:51.611 --> 01:57.450
where the Santa Ana headwinds blow
from Mexico, in search of something.

02:06.918 --> 02:11.422
EPISODE 1
STEEL BALL RUN

02:14.968 --> 02:17.636
Hey! The toilet's overflowing with poop!

02:17.637 --> 02:19.888
- This is my tent!
- Shut up, I was here first!

02:19.889 --> 02:21.265
SEPTEMBER 23, 1890
SAN DIEGO BEACH

02:21.266 --> 02:24.102
Welcome to the Steel Ball Run race!

02:28.064 --> 02:33.152
This race starts here
in San Diego and ends in New York.

02:33.153 --> 02:39.159
This is the first-ever horseback race
across the North American continent!

02:41.953 --> 02:44.746
The total distance is about 4,000 miles.

02:44.747 --> 02:47.875
The course is divided into nine stages,

02:47.876 --> 02:52.130
and the prize money
for conquering it is $50 million.

02:53.006 --> 02:58.553
Only one of the people gathered
on the beach right now will claim it.

03:01.973 --> 03:03.765
Mr. Steven Steel!

03:03.766 --> 03:08.937
Baron Roocatugo from Germany announced
he'd use a machine called an automobile.

03:08.938 --> 03:10.815
I approved it, of course.

03:11.482 --> 03:14.777
The spirit of pioneering is
part of this race's identity.

03:15.612 --> 03:19.823
No matter what kind of machine it is,
we'll take on this challenge.

03:19.824 --> 03:24.703
There's criticism that the $150 entry fee
is a money-seeking scheme.

03:24.704 --> 03:26.456
I don't think so.

03:27.332 --> 03:30.334
Because we'll cover medical
and other expenses

03:30.335 --> 03:32.544
if a participant retires.

03:32.545 --> 03:36.465
However, they must ensure
their own safety during the race.

03:36.466 --> 03:42.262
We won't violate the Second Amendment
right to bear arms and protect oneself.

03:42.263 --> 03:45.767
The race will be a total failure
if no one reaches the goal.

03:46.267 --> 03:49.395
How will you take responsibility
toward the investors?

03:50.772 --> 03:52.190
I might get killed.

03:52.815 --> 03:54.442
Just kidding.

03:55.151 --> 03:56.444
Excuse me?

03:57.111 --> 03:59.279
Failure is…

03:59.280 --> 04:00.906
Listen carefully!

04:00.907 --> 04:04.826
True failure is when
someone forgets the pioneering spirit

04:04.827 --> 04:09.415
and stays away
from ever facing challenges!

04:10.500 --> 04:13.461
In this race,
there's no such thing as failure!

04:13.962 --> 04:16.213
All we've got are adventurers!

04:16.214 --> 04:18.966
This Steel Ball Run race
will be a competition

04:18.967 --> 04:24.138
that no one in the world
has ever experienced before!

04:29.185 --> 04:34.523
What do I do? I'm so worried, you know?

04:34.524 --> 04:38.194
What do I do if it fails?

04:38.695 --> 04:40.821
Don't worry, Steven.

04:40.822 --> 04:44.117
You've been a promoter
for 40 years, haven't you?

04:45.118 --> 04:48.663
Have confidence, my dear.

04:51.082 --> 04:53.126
Okay, I'll do my best.

04:53.626 --> 04:54.919
There, there.

05:07.098 --> 05:09.851
You'd like to participate
in the race, correct?

05:11.519 --> 05:12.979
Please sign here.

05:13.563 --> 05:17.025
We'll take the horse's noseprint
and the racer's fingerprints on race day.

05:17.525 --> 05:21.070
The rider and the horse
cannot be replaced during the race.

05:21.571 --> 05:23.740
This is your entry certificate
and saddlecloth.

05:31.039 --> 05:32.999
Gyro Zeppeli.

05:34.709 --> 05:36.878
He-heh!

05:38.588 --> 05:41.758
That's a strange thing you've got there.

05:42.342 --> 05:44.802
What do you use these for?

05:46.304 --> 05:48.014
WHIRL

05:48.848 --> 05:49.682
What the…

05:54.312 --> 05:56.521
What? My legs…

05:56.522 --> 05:59.483
You bastard! What did you do?

05:59.484 --> 06:03.153
I was just a little curious
about those weird things.

06:03.154 --> 06:04.488
Is that so?

06:04.489 --> 06:07.700
Attendant, count my entry fee.

06:08.451 --> 06:12.705
If there's nothing wrong,
I'll believe what you say.

06:15.083 --> 06:17.751
Oh, you're $20 short.

06:17.752 --> 06:20.004
But I certainly paid, didn't I?

06:20.505 --> 06:24.591
I haven't issued the receipt yet.
If it's short, it's short.

06:24.592 --> 06:27.552
Then I knew it. It was you.

06:27.553 --> 06:30.472
Take out the coins you pocketed.

06:30.473 --> 06:36.854
Otherwise, I won't be able
to enter the race and win, will I?

06:38.481 --> 06:39.982
What, a thief?

06:40.483 --> 06:42.025
Security!

06:42.026 --> 06:43.736
Give me my receipt first.

06:51.869 --> 06:54.372
- What's going on?
- They say he's a pickpocket.

06:56.290 --> 06:58.459
Valkyrie, sorry to keep you waiting.

06:59.544 --> 07:02.295
- Now, which tent is mine--
- Hey!

07:02.296 --> 07:06.299
Stop right there, you bastard!
This isn't over!

07:06.300 --> 07:10.053
Don't get cocky
pulling weird shit like that.

07:10.054 --> 07:11.139
Stay still!

07:11.931 --> 07:14.142
You're dead!

07:15.393 --> 07:17.269
Hey, this idiot took my gun.

07:17.270 --> 07:18.521
You bastard!

07:21.732 --> 07:26.028
Hey, gold-teeth bastard.
If I wanted, you'd be dead right now.

07:26.654 --> 07:30.657
You never saw the moment
I took your money.

07:30.658 --> 07:33.910
You took a random guess
and tried to embarrass me!

07:33.911 --> 07:35.996
I can't let this slide anymore!

07:35.997 --> 07:40.876
I've decided! I'll join the race
and follow you all the way!

07:40.877 --> 07:43.712
Shut up!
We're turning you in to the sheriff.

07:43.713 --> 07:45.923
Let that guy go.

07:47.675 --> 07:49.426
I'm not pressing charges.

07:49.427 --> 07:51.637
Complaint withdrawn. Let him go.

07:53.514 --> 07:56.142
And give him the gun back.

08:11.032 --> 08:12.074
Pick it up.

08:12.950 --> 08:16.579
But once you do, that'll be the signal.

08:21.459 --> 08:23.001
We can't handle this.

08:23.002 --> 08:24.085
Get the sheriff!

08:24.086 --> 08:26.631
They might end up killing each other!

08:27.590 --> 08:29.174
What's all this noise?

08:29.175 --> 08:32.052
Hey! Move it, guys.

08:32.053 --> 08:33.471
I can't see.

08:42.605 --> 08:44.564
Hey!

08:44.565 --> 08:46.983
Why did you take it so seriously?

08:46.984 --> 08:49.028
I was just kidding, just kidding!

08:50.029 --> 08:53.574
Come on, don't make such a scary face.

08:54.659 --> 08:57.953
See? It was all a joke.

08:57.954 --> 09:00.455
Anyway, good luck in the race.

09:00.456 --> 09:03.251
What are you guys doing here?

09:04.544 --> 09:06.462
THUD

09:17.598 --> 09:19.350
I'm not a nice guy.

09:19.976 --> 09:22.561
Get your finger off the trigger.

09:22.562 --> 09:26.440
Then get yourself to a hospital.
Make it before lunch.

09:28.276 --> 09:30.486
You goddamn bastard!

09:39.453 --> 09:41.371
Sheriff, what do we do?

09:41.372 --> 09:44.333
It's nothing. Just a duel.

09:44.959 --> 09:48.379
A duel both sides agreed to.
Nothing wrong with that.

09:49.922 --> 09:51.673
A duel?

09:51.674 --> 09:54.385
What did that guy just do?

09:55.136 --> 09:58.096
That Steel Ball was spinning.

09:58.097 --> 09:59.014
THUD

09:59.015 --> 10:00.181
And fast.

10:00.182 --> 10:04.729
And it dug into his arm
and kept spinning even more.

10:06.105 --> 10:08.983
Hey, you! What is that Steel Ball?

10:09.483 --> 10:11.192
Let me see it again!

10:11.193 --> 10:13.195
Don't touch it! It's still spinning!

10:25.291 --> 10:27.668
What just happened?

10:28.169 --> 10:32.590
Just now,
I really was standing on my own legs.

10:36.927 --> 10:38.387
Wait!

10:39.847 --> 10:40.973
Let me through!

10:41.724 --> 10:44.768
Out of my way! Move it, you slow punk!

10:44.769 --> 10:46.936
- What did you just say?
- Shut up!

10:46.937 --> 10:48.356
Wait!

10:50.232 --> 10:53.068
Tell me! What did you just do to me?

10:53.069 --> 10:54.736
What just happened?

10:54.737 --> 10:57.406
Do you know the top cause of death?

10:58.282 --> 11:01.576
Diseases spread by mosquitoes
are number one,

11:01.577 --> 11:04.455
then getting kicked by a horse.

11:04.955 --> 11:08.167
Are you trying to switch those rankings?

11:08.751 --> 11:10.878
Don't get any weird hopes up.

11:11.587 --> 11:15.048
You standing up from that chair
was just a coincidence.

11:15.049 --> 11:17.217
It was only a physical reflex.

11:17.218 --> 11:18.094
A reflex?

11:19.136 --> 11:21.180
So it really was the Steel Ball!

11:22.056 --> 11:24.391
Show it again! I'll pay you for it.

11:24.392 --> 11:26.769
I'm done talking.

11:34.026 --> 11:37.779
Hey, brat.
You really had the nerve to do that.

11:37.780 --> 11:39.280
Well?

11:39.281 --> 11:40.157
In that case…

11:42.660 --> 11:46.872
I'll go ahead and touch it again myself!

11:56.090 --> 11:57.424
My fingers…

11:57.425 --> 12:00.302
I'll give you credit
before disappointing you.

12:00.803 --> 12:05.140
You've got some well-trained muscles
in your upper body.

12:05.141 --> 12:07.143
Now, let me make this clear.

12:07.643 --> 12:13.231
The Steel Spin won't make someone
who can't walk start walking again.

12:13.232 --> 12:15.859
Like, I'd buy that
with all that's happened!

12:15.860 --> 12:19.320
I swear I'll uncover
the truth behind that spin!

12:19.321 --> 12:21.656
Even though you can't ride a horse?

12:21.657 --> 12:23.909
I'll be gone the day after tomorrow.

12:24.577 --> 12:26.786
I've got a race to win.

12:26.787 --> 12:29.206
Hey, wait! Damn it…

12:36.005 --> 12:37.631
Move it! Out of my way!

12:38.632 --> 12:41.551
Don't come around here, you trash.

12:41.552 --> 12:44.096
Hurry up and go home now.

13:02.948 --> 13:05.701
I wonder why I came to this beach.

13:07.411 --> 13:11.081
Was it simply
to see the start of the race?

13:11.707 --> 13:12.833
Or something else?

13:16.962 --> 13:19.381
My name is Johnny Joestar.

13:19.882 --> 13:23.594
My father was a rancher
and a famous horse trainer.

13:24.094 --> 13:27.765
From the day I was born,
horses have always been by my side.

13:29.517 --> 13:32.227
Seeing the horse's muscles move
atop the saddle

13:32.228 --> 13:35.898
and hearing the hooves
strike the ground felt beautiful to me.

13:36.398 --> 13:42.071
Through their running, I felt like I could
understand horses' thoughts and emotions.

13:44.406 --> 13:46.784
People love beautiful things.

13:47.284 --> 13:52.248
And if that beautiful thing is in motion,
then it's the most beautiful thing ever.

13:53.165 --> 13:55.251
"Young Master Johnny has talent,"

13:55.835 --> 13:58.670
said an old groom, and I got encouraged.

13:58.671 --> 14:01.215
But my father never cared about me.

14:02.049 --> 14:05.469
My older brother Nicholas
was already in the spotlight.

14:07.054 --> 14:10.140
But one day, he died in an accident.

14:11.392 --> 14:13.143
Everything changed.

14:15.145 --> 14:16.479
After my brother's death,

14:16.480 --> 14:20.149
I began racing seriously,
winning over and over again.

14:20.150 --> 14:22.278
I was called a prodigy.

14:23.779 --> 14:27.156
With each victory,
more people gathered around me,

14:27.157 --> 14:30.828
flattering me from under the horse,
bringing money and gifts.

14:31.829 --> 14:34.038
Winning on horseback

14:34.039 --> 14:39.044
was a symbol of triumph
in human history and a mark of authority.

14:40.588 --> 14:43.090
But it didn't last long.

14:43.591 --> 14:47.969
So you know, Dorothy Parker is super cute!

14:47.970 --> 14:49.888
You really love her, don't you?

14:49.889 --> 14:54.642
I'm telling you, the time's coming
when cool actresses become art!

14:54.643 --> 14:58.438
- Excuse me, I'm standing in line.
- Man, look at this crowd.

14:58.439 --> 14:59.607
Oh really?

15:01.442 --> 15:03.610
I've been here since yesterday.

15:03.611 --> 15:05.361
Wow, that's amazing.

15:05.362 --> 15:10.033
The back of the line is over there!
I've been here all night!

15:10.034 --> 15:13.328
Shut up!
You're shaking after a single all-nighter!

15:13.329 --> 15:15.496
Hey, what's going on here?

15:15.497 --> 15:20.002
Hey, I was standing in line properly,
but this guy started giving me crap.

15:20.502 --> 15:23.255
This is Johnny Joestar.

15:27.760 --> 15:29.636
I knew it! You're the coolest.

15:29.637 --> 15:31.930
But is this worth lining up for?

15:31.931 --> 15:33.640
Well…

15:33.641 --> 15:34.683
BAM

15:35.517 --> 15:36.560
What's up?

15:37.144 --> 15:39.188
You're one persistent bastard.

15:44.860 --> 15:47.446
What the hell did you…

15:52.451 --> 15:54.578
Once again, everything changed.

16:00.876 --> 16:02.419
Hey, nurse.

16:02.920 --> 16:05.047
Answer me! Hey!

16:06.215 --> 16:08.509
Crap… Damn it…

16:09.218 --> 16:15.057
It's mine…
I'm shitting myself, and pissing too…

16:15.557 --> 16:20.813
Hey, hurry up and clean up my shit!
That's your job, isn't it?

16:21.313 --> 16:24.315
And what's this tube hooked up to my leg?

16:24.316 --> 16:26.110
Blood's flowing through it!

16:28.654 --> 16:31.240
Stop yelling so loudly.

16:32.366 --> 16:35.118
I'm just taking some of your blood.

16:35.119 --> 16:38.579
You can't feel anything anyway,
so it's fine, isn't it?

16:38.580 --> 16:39.915
You bastard…

16:42.710 --> 16:46.045
No one comes to visit you.

16:46.046 --> 16:48.090
Not even your old man.

16:48.841 --> 16:51.343
No one wants to look at you.

16:51.927 --> 16:56.765
You're just some former jockey prodigy
who can't even clean up his own shit!

17:00.019 --> 17:01.770
Damn it.

17:02.813 --> 17:05.107
I'll find out, no matter what.

17:05.607 --> 17:07.776
I'll ride a horse again!

17:08.277 --> 17:11.655
SEPTEMBER 24, 1890
THE DAY BEFORE THE RACE

17:13.282 --> 17:17.411
How is it, Valkyrie? See any horses
that could potentially rival you?

17:17.995 --> 17:20.205
From what I can see…

17:27.588 --> 17:29.380
He's seriously still going?

17:29.381 --> 17:31.340
He's been at it since midnight.

17:31.341 --> 17:33.718
I heard he's going to enter the race.

17:33.719 --> 17:38.765
But no matter how much of a famous jockey
he used to be, that's just sad.

17:38.766 --> 17:40.517
For the horse, that is.

17:42.853 --> 17:44.645
SLAM

17:44.646 --> 17:46.482
Hey, he's in trouble.

17:47.066 --> 17:49.567
Is he still dreaming about his past glory?

17:49.568 --> 17:51.445
He'll get seriously hurt.

17:55.199 --> 17:57.618
Yikes! Is that guy really okay?

17:58.494 --> 18:01.996
I heard he can't feel pain
'cause of what happened to his lower body.

18:01.997 --> 18:07.294
On top of that, the horse he was sold is
old, bad-tempered, and out of control.

18:08.462 --> 18:09.463
Watch.

18:12.299 --> 18:14.717
I can't watch this! Tell him to stop!

18:14.718 --> 18:16.178
You think so too, right?

18:17.012 --> 18:19.223
I was just watching.

18:19.723 --> 18:23.685
But if you ask me,
there's no way he's riding that thing.

18:24.269 --> 18:26.188
He can't ride it like that.

18:27.856 --> 18:32.861
To put it another way, if he could ride
that thing, he'd be beyond human.

18:36.573 --> 18:38.117
I want to join the race.

18:39.409 --> 18:41.869
Listen, you need to pay an entry fee.

18:41.870 --> 18:43.705
With the white man's money.

18:44.748 --> 18:46.875
Can you pay?

18:48.085 --> 18:49.169
This is…

18:50.212 --> 18:51.630
An emerald?

18:53.298 --> 18:55.424
Your certificate and saddlecloth.

18:55.425 --> 18:58.427
Before the start,
we'll take your horse's noseprint.

18:58.428 --> 19:00.806
- No need.
- What?

19:01.723 --> 19:05.853
I'll cross the continent
and win with just these legs.

19:07.146 --> 19:10.315
All I need is the white man's money.

19:15.988 --> 19:17.739
Tomorrow is finally the day.

19:30.878 --> 19:33.797
SEPTEMBER 25, 1890
RACE DAY

19:45.142 --> 19:46.351
Heh.

19:52.399 --> 19:55.318
Ladies and gentlemen,
it's finally starting.

19:55.319 --> 19:58.154
The great race across North America.

19:58.155 --> 20:00.740
Steel Ball Run!

20:00.741 --> 20:03.242
The beach is unbelievably packed

20:03.243 --> 20:06.663
with participants,
spectators, and horse poop.

20:07.664 --> 20:11.627
Now, here come the top contenders.

20:13.503 --> 20:17.548
The cowboy from Wyoming, Mountain Tim,

20:17.549 --> 20:20.802
with his beloved horse, Shadow Rider!

20:21.970 --> 20:26.349
The master horseman
from Mongolia, Dott Han!

20:26.350 --> 20:28.685
His beloved horse is Number One!

20:29.311 --> 20:32.772
The nomad from the Sahara, Urmd Avdul!

20:32.773 --> 20:35.651
Would you believe it?
He's entering on a camel!

20:36.235 --> 20:40.988
Now, appearing alongside
his beloved horse, Silver Bullet,

20:40.989 --> 20:43.699
with the saddlecloth #001,

20:43.700 --> 20:48.330
the nobleman of British horse racing,
Diego Brando!

20:51.375 --> 20:56.837
The first stage is a short ten-mile race,
with a Catholic church as the finish line.

20:56.838 --> 20:58.714
The winner of this stage

20:58.715 --> 21:02.803
will receive a one-hour time bonus
and a $10,000 prize.

21:03.303 --> 21:10.102
Let the Steel Ball Run begin!

21:14.398 --> 21:18.151
Dear distinguished guests,
after the race starts,

21:18.652 --> 21:23.781
you'll be able to follow it
on a specially prepared train.

21:23.782 --> 21:26.410
Hey, look, it's that guy.

21:30.080 --> 21:32.708
So he really is crazy, after all.

21:39.589 --> 21:41.133
Damn it…

21:43.468 --> 21:45.137
I won't give up.

21:45.637 --> 21:47.346
It's the spin…

21:47.347 --> 21:52.143
I'm going to find out the secret
of the Steel Balls, no matter what.

21:52.144 --> 21:54.771
You chose the right horse.

21:55.355 --> 21:57.190
An old horse has experience.

21:57.691 --> 22:01.611
It won't rush in like a young horse
and sprain its legs.

22:02.654 --> 22:04.948
Since I'm intrigued, here's a hint.

22:06.074 --> 22:08.993
You already have the answer.

22:08.994 --> 22:13.623
If you have the will to ride a horse,
why don't you use it?

22:15.083 --> 22:16.209
He-heh!

22:18.253 --> 22:20.589
Two minutes until the race starts.

22:26.803 --> 22:28.096
One more time…

22:28.889 --> 22:30.640
Lick me one more time.

22:36.271 --> 22:37.189
One more time…

22:39.232 --> 22:40.108
Spin!

22:44.446 --> 22:47.824
It's time to start the Steel Ball Run!

23:02.589 --> 23:06.634
September 25, 1890, 10:00 a.m.,

23:06.635 --> 23:10.388
the transcontinental race
across North America, Steel Ball Run,

23:10.389 --> 23:12.849
has finally kicked off!

23:16.061 --> 23:20.732
No way! How is he controlling it
when he can't use his legs?

23:21.983 --> 23:24.361
I can do this if I'm with you.

23:27.406 --> 23:28.698
Spin…

23:29.408 --> 23:33.161
I want to learn more
about the Steel Balls.

23:45.799 --> 23:48.634
Every horse is
neck and neck from the start.

23:48.635 --> 23:53.097
No surprise there. The first stage may
be short, but it's still ten miles.

23:53.098 --> 23:57.477
A bad pace could
wear out their horses on the first day.

23:59.020 --> 24:01.105
Someone has jumped ahead!

24:01.106 --> 24:03.566
Saddlecloth #636.

24:03.567 --> 24:07.027
He's fast! So fast!
What unbelievable speed.

24:07.028 --> 24:08.112
Who's that?

24:08.113 --> 24:11.574
636. Gyro Zeppeli.

24:11.575 --> 24:15.829
Is he out of his mind?
Running at that speed on the first day…

24:16.413 --> 24:19.373
Is he actually planning
to cross the continent?

24:19.374 --> 24:24.254
No, he said he was going to win.
He came here for that reason.

24:29.718 --> 24:30.926
We're swerving!

24:30.927 --> 24:34.264
This is bad. The other horses are
starting to get riled up.

24:36.057 --> 24:40.020
Someone is down!
Several horses may be out already!

24:43.398 --> 24:46.776
However, ramming isn't against the rules.

24:47.903 --> 24:50.988
Another horse has
broken away from the group.

24:50.989 --> 24:52.990
It's Diego Brando!

24:52.991 --> 24:56.952
The top British racing gentleman
is making his move.

24:56.953 --> 25:01.458
No, wait! Someone else is also
closing in from the left rear!

25:02.751 --> 25:06.171
It's Urmd Avdul's camel!

25:07.422 --> 25:10.090
A camel weighs
1.5 times more than a horse.

25:10.091 --> 25:14.011
No horse can withstand this attack!

25:14.012 --> 25:16.264
Gyro's tripping up!

25:16.890 --> 25:18.975
Diego Brando seizes the opening!

25:29.110 --> 25:32.947
The one getting the time bonus will be

25:32.948 --> 25:36.033
me, Urmd Avdul!

25:36.034 --> 25:37.410
BOOM

25:40.288 --> 25:41.540
What?!

25:49.422 --> 25:51.507
Avdul is down!

25:51.508 --> 25:54.594
Didn't he notice the cactus patch?

25:55.095 --> 25:57.346
Avdul is unable to move!

25:57.347 --> 26:03.019
Urmd Avdul, a top contender,
suddenly drops out in the first stage!

26:10.402 --> 26:12.696
That's Gyro's Steel Ball.

26:16.533 --> 26:19.118
I don't get how it works,

26:19.119 --> 26:21.912
but he used it to locate the cactus patch

26:21.913 --> 26:24.457
and lure the camel rider right into it.

26:25.083 --> 26:29.587
I want to know
about that Steel Ball and that guy.

26:29.588 --> 26:33.632
I'll take whatever I can get,
except diseases.

26:33.633 --> 26:35.343
And especially a time bonus.

26:35.927 --> 26:37.429
He-heh!

26:43.852 --> 26:45.353
What?

26:45.937 --> 26:48.773
What time is it?

26:51.776 --> 26:55.946
What?! Dang it! I overslept!

26:55.947 --> 26:57.656
I can't refund your entry fee.

26:57.657 --> 27:01.160
No, I'm in!
I can't win the prize money otherwise!

27:01.161 --> 27:02.453
Say what?

27:02.454 --> 27:04.705
I'm gonna win, yo!

27:04.706 --> 27:09.793
I'm a man
at the peak of my life right now!

27:09.794 --> 27:14.089
Some weirdo just started.
Write it down, just in case.

27:14.090 --> 27:16.050
Saddlecloth #777.

27:16.051 --> 27:18.094
The name's Pocoloco.

27:19.763 --> 27:22.723
This ground is incredibly smooth!

27:22.724 --> 27:24.725
With horses trampling it down,

27:24.726 --> 27:28.312
I've never seen ground
this easy to run on!

27:28.313 --> 27:33.026
Pocoloco's on a roll! Yo!

27:33.777 --> 27:35.569
I just realized something.

27:35.570 --> 27:39.615
Isn't crossing the continent
with 400 yards per liter impossible?

27:39.616 --> 27:43.828
How unfortunate.
Let's return to our homeland, Master.

27:46.956 --> 27:50.084
All right,
Gyro Zeppeli still holds the lead.

27:50.085 --> 27:53.088
Diego Brando, known as Dio,
is holding second place.

27:54.339 --> 27:57.217
That guy…
He's been moving weird for a while.

27:58.009 --> 28:01.012
Pursuing on the right,
then closing in on the left.

28:01.513 --> 28:04.516
He's closing the gap with Gyro
little by little.

28:11.898 --> 28:15.276
Again! Did he actually find it?

28:19.030 --> 28:19.989
He's gone?

28:20.490 --> 28:23.451
What just happened? Dio has disappeared!

28:24.953 --> 28:27.455
He caught up to him so suddenly!

28:29.541 --> 28:33.877
What the hell is this?
It didn't look like he was speeding up.

28:33.878 --> 28:37.047
The camel thing surprised me a little,

28:37.048 --> 28:40.467
but now I see you as a complete amateur.

28:40.468 --> 28:42.429
I can read what comes next.

28:42.929 --> 28:46.766
So he did find it! The horse's quirk!

28:47.267 --> 28:52.312
Everyone and everything
has a quirk of some sort,

28:52.313 --> 28:54.064
horses included.

28:54.065 --> 28:59.153
Tail flicks before sprinting,
drifting wide when pressured,

28:59.154 --> 29:01.739
shaking the head, lowering the body.

29:01.740 --> 29:05.118
That can sometimes be
a huge weakness in a race.

29:05.618 --> 29:08.454
This horse's quirk is a truly fatal flaw.

29:08.455 --> 29:10.289
Five, six, seven…

29:10.290 --> 29:11.708
It shifts to the left.

29:16.129 --> 29:19.591
Yes, it slightly drifts
left every eighth breath.

29:20.175 --> 29:23.135
And naturally, this shift slows it down.

29:23.136 --> 29:25.846
In other words,
if I speed up at that moment,

29:25.847 --> 29:30.518
I can match his speed
without tiring my beloved horse!

29:32.061 --> 29:33.937
DASH

29:33.938 --> 29:36.148
Dio's in front by a head!

29:36.149 --> 29:38.568
What's the meaning of this?

29:39.360 --> 29:41.236
It's a professional technique.

29:41.237 --> 29:44.072
You stay back there.

29:44.073 --> 29:48.035
Are you saying my horse has a quirk?

29:48.036 --> 29:51.622
Would it matter if I told you?
You can't fix a quirk.

29:51.623 --> 29:53.833
Just like you can't change fate!

29:56.169 --> 29:58.629
Dio's advancing again!

29:58.630 --> 30:00.422
What is this?

30:00.423 --> 30:04.510
Dio takes the lead,
but it doesn't look like he's speeding up!

30:04.511 --> 30:08.055
Natural talent. That's what that is.

30:08.056 --> 30:11.517
It's no good.
He won't be able to pass him again.

30:11.518 --> 30:13.811
The gap will keep getting bigger.

30:13.812 --> 30:17.899
The sign shows we have eight miles left.
Up ahead is a dried-up river.

30:20.443 --> 30:25.030
Hey, so you had a quirk?
I didn't know that.

30:25.031 --> 30:29.327
There are some outrageously strong rivals
out there in the world.

30:29.911 --> 30:32.539
But you don't need to fix your quirk.

30:33.122 --> 30:35.542
Run and bring it out even more.

30:42.841 --> 30:46.802
Hey, you're wobbling. Is that your quirk?

30:46.803 --> 30:49.556
That's good. Do it more.

30:50.598 --> 30:52.976
Run and bring out your quirk even more.

30:56.604 --> 30:59.189
The bridge planks are
breaking and falling!

30:59.190 --> 31:03.027
Gyro Zeppeli charges straight through!

31:04.112 --> 31:05.822
Dio hesitated!

31:06.322 --> 31:07.240
That guy…

31:07.824 --> 31:10.784
The trailing riders are going
down the river.

31:10.785 --> 31:12.579
Dio can't cross the bridge.

31:13.079 --> 31:15.789
It's just like with my legs.

31:15.790 --> 31:21.211
The mysterious Steel Ball's spin drew out
the horse's quirk in an explosive way!

31:21.212 --> 31:22.630
He-heh!

31:25.884 --> 31:30.555
There! I see them.
I caught up to the group in the back.

31:31.806 --> 31:33.849
What the… It's a cliff!

31:33.850 --> 31:35.893
This isn't the racecourse!

31:35.894 --> 31:38.146
Damn it, it's that guy's fault!

31:46.279 --> 31:50.490
He was charging ahead so fast,
we just got drawn along!

31:50.491 --> 31:52.367
But look at the map!

31:52.368 --> 31:55.078
If we cross this cliff, it's a shortcut!

31:55.079 --> 31:58.040
Only if you're okay
with your horse getting hurt.

31:58.041 --> 32:00.501
I'm turning back. Screw this.

32:04.756 --> 32:06.174
I'm…

32:09.844 --> 32:11.888
What are you doing, Pocoloco?

32:12.847 --> 32:15.725
I'm counting the clouds.

32:16.309 --> 32:22.230
What I'm asking is
why lie around all day instead of working?

32:22.231 --> 32:23.815
Three days ago,

32:23.816 --> 32:26.443
I had an old fortune-teller lady
tell my fortune.

32:26.444 --> 32:27.402
So what?

32:27.403 --> 32:32.532
She said the worst period of one's life
is called "killed by heaven."

32:32.533 --> 32:33.617
Well, listen up.

32:33.618 --> 32:37.622
She said mine's the opposite.
The opposite of the worst.

32:38.414 --> 32:43.835
Your next two months will be
the most blissful period of your life.

32:43.836 --> 32:46.713
Moreover, you're one in five billion.

32:46.714 --> 32:49.174
There's nothing to hesitate about.

32:49.175 --> 32:52.720
No enemies to fear!

32:54.472 --> 32:57.182
Then here's your lucky break.

32:57.183 --> 33:01.061
The landlord hired us
to cultivate a new field.

33:01.062 --> 33:05.565
Sorry, but I decided to take it easy.

33:05.566 --> 33:09.278
There's no such thing
as easy for people like us.

33:09.779 --> 33:13.281
I lost count of the clouds.

33:13.282 --> 33:15.575
I negotiated with the landlord

33:15.576 --> 33:19.163
and got your pay bumped
from 100 to 150, you know.

33:24.168 --> 33:27.629
Old man, that job cultivating a new field…

33:27.630 --> 33:30.383
How much did you just say it pays?

33:30.883 --> 33:34.177
I'm a one-in-five-billion guy.

33:34.178 --> 33:36.847
That belief brought me here to San Diego.

33:36.848 --> 33:39.976
I'm going to win. I'll win, and then

33:40.560 --> 33:47.275
go back home
and live an even happier life!

33:55.908 --> 33:59.412
Use the rope you have,
if you're good with it.

34:01.122 --> 34:02.498
WHOOSH

34:14.218 --> 34:17.095
What kind of legs does that guy have?

34:17.096 --> 34:19.848
But I'm not thanking him.

34:19.849 --> 34:23.770
I made it over the cliff,
thanks to my good luck.

34:24.604 --> 34:26.147
Hey ya!

34:33.362 --> 34:36.782
Only four miles left in the first stage.

34:36.783 --> 34:38.950
Gyro Zeppeli is still in the lead!

34:38.951 --> 34:41.412
Can he hold that lead till the end?!

34:43.873 --> 34:49.003
Whoa, Gyro's taking a huge detour.
What on earth is he planning to do?

34:49.879 --> 34:51.339
It's a shortcut.

34:51.923 --> 34:55.884
If he charges through the woods,
he could gain about 800 yards.

34:55.885 --> 34:58.554
But won't those trees get in the way?

34:59.138 --> 35:01.891
It's a gamble. A very dangerous one.

35:02.850 --> 35:05.685
Now, what will the chasing pack do?

35:05.686 --> 35:08.564
We can't let him get any farther ahead.

35:09.148 --> 35:12.943
One racer followed!
Then six more. Seven racers in total!

35:12.944 --> 35:16.321
Yeehaw! I caught up!

35:16.322 --> 35:17.948
Yo!

35:17.949 --> 35:20.742
Do you know where the leader is right now?

35:20.743 --> 35:24.914
Do you even realize?
We're heading straight into the woods.

35:28.584 --> 35:34.215
I see. But shortcuts have
already proven to be my lucky route.

35:35.925 --> 35:39.387
What the… This guy's eyes are closed.

35:47.937 --> 35:49.396
I'm a lucky guy.

35:49.397 --> 35:53.650
Even if I close my eyes,
there's no way I'm hitting a tree branch.

35:53.651 --> 35:57.696
What's going on? It's not surprising
for a horse to keep running.

35:57.697 --> 36:02.243
But how can the rider stay unharmed
with his eyes closed and riding like that?

36:04.245 --> 36:07.915
What's up with that guy?
Why does he have his eyes closed?

36:08.416 --> 36:11.669
Something feels off.
With guys like that, I should just…

36:13.713 --> 36:14.714
Take this!

36:25.516 --> 36:27.435
CRUNCH

36:28.936 --> 36:32.315
Two minutes since they entered the woods.
Are they about to emerge?

36:33.816 --> 36:36.109
Here comes Gyro!

36:36.110 --> 36:39.738
As expected, Gyro Zeppeli
is maintaining a huge lead.

36:39.739 --> 36:43.492
Wait, there's another horse!
And the rider is being dragged!

36:44.160 --> 36:47.787
Saddlecloth #777.
Registered name is Pocoloco.

36:47.788 --> 36:48.788
What?

36:48.789 --> 36:50.123
This is unexpected.

36:50.124 --> 36:51.625
By being dragged along,

36:51.626 --> 36:54.921
he avoided the branches
and let his horse run freely!

36:56.380 --> 36:58.591
Was that fall actually lucky?

37:01.969 --> 37:05.055
I knew it! I'm truly a lucky guy!

37:05.056 --> 37:08.141
What the… Is that even allowed?

37:08.142 --> 37:10.060
Pocoloco is currently second.

37:10.061 --> 37:12.854
We can see the others
on the official route,

37:12.855 --> 37:15.065
but the gap is a few hundred yards.

37:15.066 --> 37:17.150
This position's not bad.

37:17.151 --> 37:18.903
The shortcut paid off.

37:19.528 --> 37:23.114
Incredible! The first stage
has been totally thrilling!

37:23.115 --> 37:26.368
And ahead is
the toughest part of the course,

37:26.369 --> 37:28.620
a 2,000-yard downhill stretch

37:28.621 --> 37:32.958
with a 50-yard drop
and slopes as steep as 30 degrees.

37:32.959 --> 37:34.084
Two thousand?

37:34.085 --> 37:39.048
Laying the rails was difficult,
so sadly, the train has to take a detour.

37:43.886 --> 37:46.972
Now, they're facing
the tricky downhill stretch.

37:46.973 --> 37:50.893
Needless to say, going too fast
will wreck their horses' legs.

37:51.477 --> 37:53.937
Every racer is holding steady.

37:53.938 --> 37:57.649
How they can hold steady
largely depends on a rider's skill!

37:57.650 --> 38:01.069
Take it slow. Careful here.

38:01.070 --> 38:04.657
Are you scared, Mr. One-in-Five-Billion?

38:06.784 --> 38:09.369
Who was that? Who said I'm scared?

38:09.370 --> 38:12.247
There's nothing to hesitate about.

38:12.248 --> 38:15.458
No enemies to fear!

38:15.459 --> 38:16.793
That's right.

38:16.794 --> 38:19.463
If there are no enemies to fear,

38:20.047 --> 38:22.675
then there's no road
to fear either, right?

38:25.469 --> 38:26.469
BAM

38:26.470 --> 38:28.222
Out of the way, old man!

38:28.723 --> 38:31.766
Pocoloco's breaking out!
He couldn't hold back!

38:31.767 --> 38:33.269
Go!

38:34.729 --> 38:37.398
Okay, he's just an idiot.

38:39.483 --> 38:42.068
Calm down. Don't be misled!

38:42.069 --> 38:47.033
They're following suit! Some of the horses
couldn't help but follow suit!

38:51.620 --> 38:54.372
This is terrible! It's a massive crash.

38:54.373 --> 38:56.583
There's a devil loose on this slope.

38:56.584 --> 38:58.877
It's okay! Keep going!

38:58.878 --> 39:00.211
We're lucky guys--

39:00.212 --> 39:02.256
JOLT

39:04.133 --> 39:05.050
WHAM

39:05.051 --> 39:08.053
Pocoloco's down! Gyro takes the lead!

39:08.054 --> 39:09.804
Nice work, pal!

39:09.805 --> 39:13.100
Pocoloco was foolish after all!

39:14.810 --> 39:16.187
What in the world?!

39:17.396 --> 39:18.313
What?

39:18.314 --> 39:21.775
Pocoloco is unharmed!
He hasn't even fallen!

39:21.776 --> 39:25.071
He's riding something,
and it's unbelievably fast!

39:26.614 --> 39:28.073
This guy…

39:28.074 --> 39:30.200
It's a dead body!

39:30.201 --> 39:32.577
He's sliding down on a cow's corpse!

39:32.578 --> 39:37.040
Yeehaw! Can't believe there was
a dead cow in the grass!

39:37.041 --> 39:38.583
I'm blown away!

39:38.584 --> 39:40.251
Pocoloco takes the lead!

39:40.252 --> 39:43.463
What is this ridiculous situation?

39:43.464 --> 39:46.300
Could it be some kind of ability?

39:46.926 --> 39:50.011
That doesn't matter right now.

39:50.012 --> 39:50.929
RUMBLE

39:50.930 --> 39:52.723
This race is meant for horses.

39:53.391 --> 39:56.810
You can't hop on a dead cow!

39:56.811 --> 39:58.104
Take this!

39:59.021 --> 40:00.271
CRASH

40:00.272 --> 40:05.152
I'll get that rock rolling
and stop the cow from sliding.

40:08.322 --> 40:11.075
What? Why is there a person there?

40:13.327 --> 40:15.161
Damn it, I missed.

40:15.162 --> 40:16.913
I can't believe my eyes!

40:16.914 --> 40:20.417
Saddlecloth #990,
Sand Man, has suddenly burst in!

40:20.418 --> 40:22.627
Shockingly, he's joining in on foot!

40:22.628 --> 40:24.672
The downhill slope is almost over.

40:26.882 --> 40:30.301
We're now over 17 minutes into the race!

40:30.302 --> 40:31.554
Damn it…

40:34.223 --> 40:36.683
Now, the final turn is in sight.

40:36.684 --> 40:39.770
After that rocky hill,
it's just a straight line!

40:40.271 --> 40:43.858
Wow! Sand Man is taking
a shortcut through the rocks!

40:46.444 --> 40:50.155
What's going on? I can't believe
things turned out like this.

40:50.156 --> 40:52.490
Is he even human?

40:52.491 --> 40:54.994
This is the natives' unknown power.

40:55.744 --> 40:59.664
A power perfectly suited
for a race across the continent.

40:59.665 --> 41:03.835
The back group finishes the descent
and heads for the final turn.

41:03.836 --> 41:06.964
Pocoloco is leading all 3,800 racers!

41:09.175 --> 41:15.889
Hey, Valkyrie, we'll never win
if we keep staring at their butts.

41:15.890 --> 41:17.391
Let's run.

41:20.186 --> 41:23.063
There he goes! Gyro's making his move!

41:24.023 --> 41:25.732
But isn't it too early?

41:25.733 --> 41:30.362
There's a 2,000-yard straightaway
after this turn!

41:42.333 --> 41:45.293
- Huh? So many people…
- Steel Ball Run!

41:45.294 --> 41:48.296
- Wow! It's a huge crowd!
- Steel Ball Run!

41:48.297 --> 41:50.590
The Santa Ana winds blow from Mexico

41:50.591 --> 41:53.718
toward the church
at the end of the desolate plains!

41:53.719 --> 41:58.932
Tens of thousands are flocking
to see the finish of the first stage!

41:58.933 --> 42:03.145
The winner of this race
will become a hero of the world.

42:06.357 --> 42:10.693
After running this far,
you've saved your strength well.

42:10.694 --> 42:13.948
We can do it. The final 2,000 yards.

42:15.533 --> 42:18.994
What? I can't believe it.
Who's that racer?

42:19.495 --> 42:20.828
It's Dio!

42:20.829 --> 42:25.042
Dio, who should've fallen far behind,
is now leading the chase!

42:29.838 --> 42:33.092
That's the wind resistance shield method!

42:33.717 --> 42:35.803
So he used this method to catch up.

42:36.303 --> 42:41.015
Winning the race or prize money
doesn't matter to me.

42:41.016 --> 42:46.939
But to uncover the mystery of Steel Balls,
I must make him acknowledge me.

42:47.439 --> 42:50.943
The one who will surpass Gyro Zeppeli…

42:52.987 --> 42:55.864
is me, Johnny Joestar!

42:57.908 --> 43:01.286
From here on out,
techniques seem to be useless.

43:01.287 --> 43:05.456
Only the strength left
in the legs matters for victory!

43:05.457 --> 43:08.167
I saved my horse's energy on the hill.

43:08.168 --> 43:10.044
The real race starts here.

43:10.045 --> 43:13.132
With less than 1,000 yards to go,
Pocoloco makes his move.

43:14.133 --> 43:16.884
Wow, Sand Man joins in too!

43:16.885 --> 43:17.802
WHOOSH

43:17.803 --> 43:19.262
It's that guy again.

43:19.263 --> 43:23.016
Five hundred yards to go.
The pursuers are charging fiercely.

43:23.017 --> 43:26.644
Dio and another rider,
saddlecloth #939, Johnny Joestar!

43:26.645 --> 43:30.315
They're seven lengths from Gyro.
Gyro is three lengths from Sand Man.

43:30.316 --> 43:33.151
Four racers are charging up on Sand Man!

43:33.152 --> 43:37.072
The pursuers are closing in on Gyro,
three lengths, two, one…

43:39.199 --> 43:41.743
They're neck and neck!

43:41.744 --> 43:44.162
Four horses are neck and neck!

43:44.163 --> 43:46.914
Johnny Joestar, I'm amazed.

43:46.915 --> 43:49.209
You've really caught up this far.

43:49.710 --> 43:53.379
By the way,
have you ever sailed on a ship?

43:53.380 --> 43:57.425
A ship goes faster
when it catches headwinds.

43:57.426 --> 44:02.639
The headwind from Mexico is meant
to help our horses run faster.

44:02.640 --> 44:04.516
From the very beginning.

44:05.601 --> 44:08.227
It's an intense showdown at the finish!

44:08.228 --> 44:11.065
Only 100 yards left!
Who will come in first?

44:14.693 --> 44:16.612
It's Gyro Zeppeli!

44:18.280 --> 44:20.698
Gyro is in the lead!

44:20.699 --> 44:22.575
Here he comes to take the lead!

44:22.576 --> 44:23.994
Those are the Steel Balls!

44:24.578 --> 44:30.041
He used the spin to spread his cloak
and gain lift by Bernoulli's principle.

44:30.042 --> 44:34.129
Just like a ship facing
the headwind from Mexico!

44:34.755 --> 44:37.215
Gyro is in the lead!

44:37.216 --> 44:39.634
Fifty yards to the goal! Thirty yards!

44:39.635 --> 44:43.472
No one can catch up to him!
Gyro Zeppeli is taking the lead and…

44:45.432 --> 44:47.267
he crossed the finish line!

44:48.936 --> 44:52.772
Gyro Zeppeli takes
the crown for the first stage!

44:52.773 --> 44:58.362
The race leader
of the Steel Ball Run is born!

44:59.655 --> 45:02.157
The summer of 1890.

45:02.658 --> 45:05.536
I was drawn here by something.

45:06.203 --> 45:09.957
Something beautiful
that was visible in the darkness.

45:10.457 --> 45:13.585
Maybe it was the light called "hope."

45:14.670 --> 45:18.716
This story is
about me taking my first steps.

45:19.425 --> 45:25.180
Not physically, but in the sense
of growing from youth into adulthood.

